# A people directory supplies its class and property hierarchy in one graph.
# --owl2rl infers Alice's types, Bob's type and the broader contact relation.
# Shows the RDFS rules included in OWL 2 RL, compiled to standalone Logic Script.
# Semantics: W3C RDF Schema, https://www.w3.org/TR/rdf-schema/

@prefix : <https://example.org/people#> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

# Class membership follows both levels of this hierarchy.
:Researcher rdfs:subClassOf :Employee .
:Employee rdfs:subClassOf :Person .

# Using colleague also implies knows and types both ends of the relation.
:colleague rdfs:subPropertyOf :knows ;
    rdfs:domain :Employee ;
    rdfs:range :Person .

# The directory supplies only Alice's specific type and her colleague link.
:Alice a :Researcher ; :colleague :Bob .
